      "side": 1,
      "message": "I get why we\u0027re putting this here (to block arbitrary map and unmapping), but are we actually getting buffers that are GpuOnly? Usually GpuOnly infers the buffer will use memory that is most optimal to read on the GPU. Do we get that guarantee with Dawn if we are also premapping the buffer? Like especially for static buffers would it be better to have premapped transfer buffer that copies into a real GpuOnly buffer?\n\nI guess this is a little hard to reason about on native GPU Apis since the idea of a one time map is really a thing.\n\nDoes it make sense to just have a different access type? Not exactly sure what that would be exactly though.",
